2026-11-27T10:45:35+10:30 | Claude chunk click | found | Rules as implemented (BoardPage.razor.cs ItemClick): plain click on a card, list row or calendar bar makes the selection exactly that item (clear + add; with the side menu expanded it also examines); a plain click on the item that is the whole selection opens it (OpenItem); a double-click opens it once (e.Detail >= 2 plus an openedByClick guard, no @ondblclick needed); Shift/Ctrl/Cmd-click toggles; a click on empty space (board/list wrapper, calendar background) clears the selection.\nWhy Roadmap.razor is touched: the calendar had no selection at all and its OnOpen carried only (root, id). It now passes the MouseEventArgs (modifiers, click count) and takes a SelectedOf func to draw a "selected" class on bars and left rows (CSS .rm-bar.selected, .rm-row.selected in app.css). The list title button lost its own click handler: the row handler (RowRender) now takes every click.\nVerified so far over CDP on the hidden desktop: board (light+dark) all steps OK; list and calendar steps OK for click/click/shift/open/dblclick, calendar modifier fix (itemClicked) rebuilt and re-run. Still running: empty-space step for list and calendar (my first spots were outside the 1280px window), then screenshot review.
